# pulse starter: todo-api ({{.Lang}})

A real CRUD API on one table — no queues, no schema beyond the key.
One small file per operation:

```
services/create-todo/     POST /todos              → 201 the new todo
services/list-todos/      GET /todos               → 200 all todos
services/complete-todo/   POST /todos/{id}/done    → 200 updated (404 if absent)
services/delete-todo/     DELETE /todos/{id}       → 204
```

The whole loop:

```bash
pulse start
curl -X POST localhost:3000/todos -d '{"text":"buy milk"}'    # note the id
curl localhost:3000/todos
curl -X POST localhost:3000/todos/<id>/done
curl -X DELETE localhost:3000/todos/<id>
```

Worth reading: `complete-todo` uses a **ConditionExpression** to return a
clean 404 instead of silently creating a row — the standard trick for
"update only if it exists". Data survives restarts; `pulse list` shows the
item count.

pulse points the vanilla AWS SDK at its local mocks via `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL`,
so this code runs unmodified in real AWS.

Prefer the other language? `pulse init <name> --template todo-api --lang node|python`
